===TRAVERSE-SKILL===
---
name: traverse
description: Conduct one bp3 quest from the main session — read state with bp3 q r, dispatch the one step that state calls for, re-read, until the quest is terminal or a human decision is owed.
---

# Traverse

Use when a human in a bp3-enabled repo invokes this skill by
name (`/traverse <quest>`, `$traverse <quest>`) or asks to "traverse",
"run", or "keep going on" a named quest until it lands or
blocks. One quest per traverse. One output: step dispatches
through `bp3 q`, ending in a traverse report — what reached
`exp_fin`, what is blocked, and what human decision is owed
next. Finish lines have report words: `exp_fin` names an exp
whose state is `landed` (its `land` edge taken); `quest_fin`
names quest promotion to master, the only owner-gated finish
line. The FSM states stay `landed`; `exp_fin`/`quest_fin`
name the finish lines in reports, never new edges.

Use `quest` instead to frame a new quest. Use `using-bp3`
instead for a single state operation by hand (one handoff, one
grade, recovery after a dead session). Use
`red-ink-quest-landing-demo` instead when the quest is done and the
human wants the landing writeup. A design under review is
`red-ink`'s job, not a traverse.

## Conductor rule

This skill is the conductor: it owns the loop and nothing
else. It reads state, dispatches the one step the state calls
for, and re-reads. It never does a step's work itself, never
calls a verdict edge for a step, and never re-judges a grade
matrix — it quotes the matrix verbatim. Legality is `bp3 q`'s
call, never this skill's: a refusal is information, answered by
re-reading, not by arguing or retrying unchanged.

Cycles are weather; blocks are decisions. A `needs_fix`
verdict below the cycle cap is weather: the conductor rides
it (Procedure step 3) without paging the owner. `blocked` is
the only page: it means a decision only a human can make is
owed. Fake blocks train rubber-stamps; never manufacture one
out of a cycle.

## No-human variant

With no human present, the `traverse-no-human` skill
runs this same conductor over a queue of quests under
no-human rails: preflight before queueing, desks only,
blocked work parks in the inbox instead of paging, a
stated Run budget stops the queue, and the run ends in
the dawn report. No-human never attests (`BP3_DECIDER`
stays unset), never takes `resume` or `delete`, and
never promotes — `quest_fin` stays the owner gate. The
rails live in `skills/traverse-no-human/SKILL.md`;
this section names the variant only, so the procedure
above stays the one conductor procedure.

## Procedure

1. Take exactly one argument: the quest. Confirm the engine
   exists: `bp3 q r <quest>` must answer JSON. If `bp3 q` is
   unavailable, stop and say so — never improvise state with
   file edits or another command.
2. Read the world live: `bp3 q r <quest>` gives exp states,
   the railway order, and the blocked inbox. Trust only this
   read — never session memory, `state.yaml`, or a ledger read
   by hand. At a fan-out group, stop and ask the human which
   members run; members are exploration only and never
   landable.
2.5. Quest worktree, by default: before the first dispatch,
   `./bin/bp3 harness desk prepare --quest <quest>` and pass its
   `path` as `desk` in every step's args. All step children
   work in that one worktree for the whole quest; the
   conductor's checkout is never worked in, so parallel
   traverses and the owner's own work cannot collide with the
   Run. If the desk cannot be prepared, stop and say so —
   never fall back to the shared tree. Release it only at
   `quest_fin` or on the owner's word (`bp3 harness desk
   release --quest <quest>`; a dirty desk refuses and is
   preserved).
3. Dispatch exactly one step per read, by state only:

   | State | Dispatch | Args |
   |---|---|---|
   | `todo` | `node-loop` workflow | `{quest, exp, ts, harness, model, desk}` |
   | `handed_off` | `induct-grade` workflow | `{quest, exp, ts, harness, model, commit, desk}` with `commit` from this read |
   | `approved` | `quest-land` workflow | `{quest, exp, ts, harness, model, desk}` |
   | `blocked` | human gate (step 4) | — |
   | `landed` / `deleted` | none | advance to the next exp, or report at terminal (`landed` is reported as `exp_fin`) |

   `ts` is a UTC compact timestamp (for example
   `20261107T143022Z`) supplied in args because workflow
   scripts cannot read the clock; `harness` and `model` carry
   this session's identity (`muse-code` and its model),
   because workflow children do not inherit the launching
   session's env. Steps are installed with this skill by
   `bp3 skills install`; if a named step is missing, stop and
   say so rather than improvising children. Grade replay is
   free: re-dispatching `induct-grade` on the same `commit`
   is always safe, so a killed grade is simply dispatched
   again — no attempt bookkeeping here.

   Cycle autonomy: when a grade returns `needs_fix` (or a
   verify returns `fail`) and the re-read shows the exp back
   in `todo` below the cycle cap, the conductor dispatches
   the next author cycle itself, carrying the grader's
   named fix — including any regression test or acceptance
   amendment that fix demands — in the next dispatch's
   context. It does not ask the owner about the cycle, does
   not wait for an owner answer, and does not present the
   cycle as a decision. The named fix rides along verbatim;
   the conductor never re-judges it, widens it, or drops it.
   It keeps dispatching grade → author → grade until the exp
   leaves the cycle (`landed`, `blocked`, or `deleted`) or
   the cap is hit. When the re-read shows the cycle cap
   reached (the exp in `blocked` at the cap), the conductor
   stops looping and escalates to the owner through the
   blocked gate instead of dispatching another cycle.
4. Blocked gate (the only page): present the inbox in the
   main session (exp, reason, checkpoint, cycle), capture
   the human's decision in their words, attest it
   (`BP3_DECIDER=human`), and take `resume` or `delete`
   through `bp3 q <quest> u <exp>`. The human never calls bp3
   and never supplies a commit. A blocked Run is never
   resumed in place; after a `resume`, the next read
   dispatches a fresh step. Only human-only calls reach
   this gate: scope changes, `delete`, and moves touching
   another quest's state. The conductor never takes a
   `delete` or a scope change autonomously, at any cycle.
5. Re-read after every dispatch return (`bp3 q r <quest>`)
   and go to step 3. A return that moved nothing (refusal, no
   commit) is re-judged from the fresh read, never retried
   unchanged against a moved tip.
6. Stop when the rollup is terminal (every exp `landed` or
   `deleted`) or a human decision is owed that this session
   cannot get. Name each `landed` exp `exp_fin` in the
   report; when the quest is promoted to master, name that
   finish line `quest_fin` (owner gate, demo first). Report: dispatches per exp with their ledger
   evidence, the grade matrices quoted verbatim, Runs and
   tapes left behind, scorecard fields (wall time, context
   tokens, human-active minutes — or "unmeasured", never
   zero), and the next decision owed.

## Rules

- The skill writes no state. `bp3 q u` is the only writer,
  called by step children (and at the blocked gate, by this
  session on attested human words); ledger files, `state.yaml`,
  and branch tips are never hand-edited, and tape is evidence,
  never parsed into facts.
- Human attestation comes only from actual human words in
  this session. The engine never attests on the human's
  behalf, and `resume` without it is refused
  (`E_HUMAN_REQUIRED`) — that refusal is the gate working.
  Attestation is owed at the blocked gate only; a
  `needs_fix` cycle below the cap needs no attestation,
  because no human decision is being recorded.
- Identity rides env (`BP3_HARNESS`, `BP3_MODEL`) set per Run
  by the launcher or hooks. Unset means `unknown` plus a
  warning in the verdict; never guess a model name.
- Verdicts bind the exact commit reviewed. A verdict naming a
  superseded commit is refused; dispatch a fresh step against
  the current commit instead of arguing with the refusal.
- Instructions only: this skill holds no state, spawns no
  daemon, and assumes no runtime beyond the main session, its
  workflow children, and the `bp3 q` binary.
===traverse.sh===
#!/bin/sh
# traverse workflow contract tests (mock host, no agent calls).
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
node test/node-loop.test.mjs
node test/induct-grade.test.mjs
node test/quest-land.test.mjs
===node-loop.test===
// Mock-host test for skills/traverse/workflows/node-loop.js.
// Covers the exp Acceptance table for the slimmed build-only
// step: the launcher's record-init writer precedes the author
// child on a todo exp (mvp.8; a refused write spawns nothing),
// only the author child spawns on a todo exp, the launcher's
// bind step follows the author (followup.3: find-tape resolves
// the session tape, bind-tape binds it; a refused resolution
// binds nothing), the file carries no other stage's edge
// commands, a handed_off exp is refused with zero stage
// children (state untouched), and the env-set run-id still
// holds for the author.
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import workflow from "../skills/traverse/workflows/node-loop.js";

const TS = "20260101T000000Z";
let failures = 0;
function assert(cond, msg) {
  if (!cond) { console.error("FAIL: " + msg); failures++; }
}

function mockHost({ reads, initFails, bindFails }) {
  let readIdx = 0;
  const labels = [];
  const inputs = {};
  const inits = [];
  const binds = [];
  const host = {
    args: { quest: "toy", exp: "fx", ts: TS, harness: "muse-code", model: "test-model" },
    async agent({ label, input }) {
      if (input.includes("harness record-init")) {
        labels.push("init");
        inputs.init = input;
        const m = input.match(/--run-id (\S+)/);
        inits.push(m ? m[1] : "");
        if (initFails) {
          return JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: { code: "E_EXISTS" } });
        }
        return JSON.stringify({ ok: true, run_id: m ? m[1] : "", harness: "muse-code" });
      }
      if (input.includes("harness find-tape")) {
        labels.push("resolve");
        inputs.resolve = input;
        if (bindFails) {
          return JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: { code: "E_AMBIGUOUS" } });
        }
        const m = input.match(/--run-id (\S+)/);
        return JSON.stringify({ ok: true, run_id: m ? m[1] : "", tape_path: "/tmp/session-tape.jsonl", wal: "/tmp/session-tape.jsonl" });
      }
      if (input.includes("harness bind-tape")) {
        labels.push("bind");
        inputs.bind = input;
        const m = input.match(/--tape-path ([^\s`]+)/);
        binds.push(m ? m[1] : "");
        const r = input.match(/--run-id (\S+)/);
        return JSON.stringify({ ok: true, run_id: r ? r[1] : "", tape_path: m ? m[1] : "" });
      }
      if (input.startsWith("Run exactly")) {
        return JSON.stringify(reads[Math.min(readIdx++, reads.length - 1)]);
      }
      const edge = label.split(" ")[0];
      labels.push(edge);
      inputs[edge] = input;
      return JSON.stringify({ ok: true, run_id: "r-" + edge, commit: "abc1234", verdict: { ok: true } });
    },
    async parallel(calls) {
      const out = [];
      for (const c of calls) out.push(await host.agent(c));
      return out;
    },
  };
  return { host, labels, inputs, inits, binds };
}

const todo = { state: "todo", cycle: 1, commit: null, legal_edges: ["handoff"] };
const handedOff = { state: "handed_off", cycle: 1, commit: "abc1234", legal_edges: ["grade", "verify"] };

// --- todo: the writer records first, the author runs, the binder follows ---
{
  const { host, labels, inputs, inits, binds } = mockHost({ reads: [todo, handedOff] });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "handed_off", "todo build hands off, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(result.commit === "abc1234", "commit comes from the re-read, got " + result.commit);
  assert(labels.join(",") === "init,author,resolve,bind", "writer, author, then bind step, got " + labels.join(","));
  assert(inits.join(",") === TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1",
    "InitRecord names the author's run-id, got " + inits.join(","));
  assert(inputs.init.includes("harness record-init --run-id " + TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1"),
    "writer calls record-init for the author run-id");
  assert(inputs.init.includes("--harness muse-code") && inputs.init.includes("--quest toy") && inputs.init.includes("--exp fx"),
    "writer records harness, quest, and exp");
  assert(!inputs.init.includes("--tape-path"),
    "writer names no tape pre-spawn; the session tape is bound after the child returns");
  assert(inputs.resolve.includes("harness find-tape --run-id " + TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1"),
    "binder resolves the author's session tape mechanically");
  assert(inputs.bind.includes("harness bind-tape --run-id " + TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1"),
    "binder calls bind-tape for the author run-id");
  assert(inputs.bind.includes("--tape-path /tmp/session-tape.jsonl"),
    "binder binds the resolved session tape");
  assert(binds.join(",") === "/tmp/session-tape.jsonl",
    "exactly one binding, for the resolved tape, got " + binds.join(","));
  const input = inputs.author;
  const want = "BP3_RUN_ID=" + TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1";
  assert(input.includes(want), "author command carries " + want);
  assert(input.includes("BP3_QUEST=toy") && input.includes("BP3_EXP=fx"),
    "author prefix carries quest/exp");
  assert(input.includes("runs/" + TS + "-handoff-muse-code-test-model-c1"),
    "handoff run folder matches BP3_RUN_ID");
  assert(!input.includes("Prefix your FIRST"),
    "author brief carries no first-command prefix instruction");
  assert(input.includes("arrive via environment"),
    "author is told the run-id arrives via environment");
  assert(input.includes("u fx handoff --commit"), "author calls the handoff edge");
  assert(result.run_ids.join(",") === "r-author", "run_ids collect the author, got " + result.run_ids.join(","));
}

// --- handed_off: refuses cleanly, no stage child, state untouched ---
{
  const { host, labels } = mockHost({ reads: [handedOff] });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "refused", "handed_off exp is refused, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(labels.length === 0, "no stage child spawns for handed_off");
  assert(result.refusals.some((r) => r.includes("handed_off")), "refusal names the state");
}

// --- approved and landed also refuse: another step owns them ---
for (const state of ["approved", "landed", "blocked"]) {
  const s = { state: state, cycle: 1, commit: "abc1234", legal_edges: [] };
  const { host, labels } = mockHost({ reads: [s] });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "refused", state + " is refused, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(labels.length === 0, "no stage child spawns for " + state);
}

// --- author makes no progress: refused, never loops ---
{
  const { host, labels } = mockHost({ reads: [todo, todo] });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "refused", "no-progress author is refused, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(labels.join(",") === "init,author,resolve,bind", "author ran exactly once, then the bind step, got " + labels.join(","));
}

// --- tape resolution refuses: nothing is bound, refusal is typed ---
{
  const { host, labels, binds } = mockHost({ reads: [todo, handedOff], bindFails: true });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "handed_off", "bind refusal does not unhand the exp, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(labels.join(",") === "init,author,resolve", "no bind child after a refused resolution, got " + labels.join(","));
  assert(binds.length === 0, "a refused resolution binds nothing, got " + binds.join(","));
  assert(result.refusals.some((r) => r.includes("bind-tape")), "refusal names bind-tape");
}

// --- writer refused: the child never starts ---
{
  const { host, labels } = mockHost({ reads: [todo, todo], initFails: true });
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "refused", "writer refusal refuses the step, got " + result.outcome);
  assert(labels.join(",") === "init", "no author spawns after a refused InitRecord, got " + labels.join(","));
  assert(result.refusals.some((r) => r.includes("record-init")), "refusal names record-init");
}

// --- missing args refuse without spawning anything ---
{
  const host = {
    args: { quest: "toy" },
    async agent() { throw new Error("must not spawn"); },
    async parallel() { throw new Error("must not spawn"); },
  };
  const result = await workflow(host);
  assert(result.outcome === "refused", "missing args refuse");
}

// --- stage set is finite: no other stage's prompts in the file ---
{
  const src = readFileSync(new URL("../skills/traverse/workflows/node-loop.js", import.meta.url), "utf8");
  assert(!src.includes("host.parallel"), "no parallel stage fan-out in the file");
  assert(!src.includes("grade --verdict"), "no grade prompt in the file");
  assert(!src.includes("verify --verdict"), "no verify prompt in the file");
  assert(!src.includes(" land --reason"), "no land prompt in the file");
  assert(!src.includes("for (let stage"), "no stage loop in the file");
}

if (failures > 0) process.exit(1);
console.log("node-loop tests: ok");
===node-loop.js===
// node-loop: build one todo exp, then stop. Installed to
// .agents/workflows/node-loop.js by `bp3 skills install`.
// This step owns exactly one transition family: it reads state,
// spawns the single author child for a `todo` exp, re-reads, and
// returns what the re-read reports. Any other state belongs to
// a different step; this file refuses it untouched. All state
// moves through `bp3 q u`, called directly by the author child;
// this script never writes state. Its one write is proof, not
// state: as the named InitRecord writer (mvp.8) it records the
// child's InitRecord via `bp3 harness record-init` before the
// child spawns; the child never writes its own proof. As the
// named tape binder (followup.3) it then binds the child's
// session tape via `bp3 harness bind-tape` after the child
// returns; the child writes no InitRecord, binding, or
// observation.
// Args are supplied by the calling traverse skill as {quest, exp,
// ts, harness, model}; ts is a UTC compact timestamp from the
// caller, embedded by the child in its run-id because scripts
// cannot read the clock.

function textOf(result) {
  if (typeof result === "string") return result;
  if (!result || typeof result !== "object") return "";
  if (typeof result.output === "string") return result.output;
  if (typeof result.text === "string") return result.text;
  if (typeof result.content === "string") return result.content;
  try {
    return JSON.stringify(result);
  } catch (e) {
    return "";
  }
}

function parseVerdict(result) {
  const text = textOf(result);
  if (!text) return null;
  try {
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (e) {
    // fall through to embedded-JSON extraction
  }
  const start = text.indexOf("{");
  const end = text.lastIndexOf("}");
  if (start >= 0 && end > start) {
    try {
      return JSON.parse(text.slice(start, end + 1));
    } catch (e) {
      return null;
    }
  }
  return null;
}

function errorText(result) {
  const v = parseVerdict(result);
  if (v && v.error && v.error.code) {
    const facts = v.error.facts ? JSON.stringify(v.error.facts) : "";
    return v.error.code + (facts ? " " + facts : "");
  }
  const text = textOf(result).trim();
  return text ? text.slice(0, 500) : "no verdict returned";
}

export default async function workflow(host) {
  const rawArgs = typeof host.args === "string"
    ? JSON.parse(host.args)
    : (host.args || {});
  const quest = rawArgs.quest;
  const exp = rawArgs.exp;
  const ts = rawArgs.ts;
  const harness = rawArgs.harness || "muse-code";
  const model = rawArgs.model || "unknown";
  const desk = rawArgs.desk ? String(rawArgs.desk) : "";
  const envPrefix =
    "BP3_HARNESS=" + harness + " BP3_MODEL=" + model + " ";
  const deskNote = desk ? ("Your working directory is the quest worktree `" + desk + "` - cd there first and run every command from there; do not work in the conductor checkout. ") : "";
  const authorLoad =
    "First load the code-writer skill (read_skill \"code-writer\") " +
    "and follow its procedure, including naming discipline and " +
    "its language references. ";
  const refusals = [];
  const runIds = [];
  if (!quest || !exp || !ts) {
    return {
      exp: exp || null,
      outcome: "refused",
      commit: null,
      run_ids: runIds,
      refusals: ["missing quest, exp, or ts in workflow args"],
    };
  }

  const expDir =
    "docs/quests/" + quest + "/experiments/" + exp;

  async function readState() {
    const result = await host.agent({
      label: "read " + exp,
      input:
        "Run exactly `" + envPrefix + "./bin/bp3 q " + quest + " r " + exp +
        "` from the quest worktree if one is named below, else the repository root, and return only its stdout JSON " +
        "verdict verbatim as your entire reply, with no prose and no " +
        "code fences. If the command fails, return its stdout JSON " +
        "verdict verbatim instead. Do not edit any file and do not " +
        "call any `bp3 q u` update edge.",
    });
    const v = parseVerdict(result);
    if (!v || typeof v.state !== "string") {
      return {
        state: "unknown",
        commit: null,
        cycle: 0,
        legal_edges: [],
        raw: textOf(result),
      };
    }
    return {
      state: v.state,
      commit: v.commit === undefined ? null : v.commit,
      cycle: typeof v.cycle === "number" ? v.cycle : 0,
      legal_edges: Array.isArray(v.legal_edges) ? v.legal_edges : [],
      raw: textOf(result),
    };
  }

  function runFolder(edge, cycle, harnessNote) {
    return (
      expDir + "/runs/" + ts + "-" + edge + "-" + harnessNote +
      "-c" + String(cycle)
    );
  }

  function envPreset(edge, cycle) {
    // Env-set identity: BP3_RUN_ID carries the same id as this
    // stage's run folder. `bp3` reads it from the environment
    // and stamps it into verdicts and ledger lines, so no
    // first-command prefix binds the session.
    return (
      "BP3_RUN_ID=" + ts + "-" + edge + "-" + harness + "-" + model +
      "-c" + String(cycle) + " BP3_QUEST=" + quest + " BP3_EXP=" +
      exp + " " + envPrefix
    );
  }

  function runIdOf(edge, cycle) {
    return ts + "-" + edge + "-" + harness + "-" + model +
      "-c" + String(cycle);
  }

  // The named InitRecord writer (mvp.8): this launcher, before
  // the child spawns. The child never writes its own proof; a
  // refused write means the child never starts. The record
  // names no tape (followup.3): the child's session tape does
  // not exist yet, so the launcher binds it after the child
  // returns (bindTape below). The run folder's tape.log stays
  // the child's own transcript, never finish evidence.
  async function recordInit(edge, cycle) {
    const cmd =
      envPreset(edge, cycle) + "./bin/bp3 harness record-init" +
      " --run-id " + runIdOf(edge, cycle) +
      " --harness " + harness + " --quest " + quest +
      " --exp " + exp + " --model " + model +
      (desk ? " --desk " + desk : "");
    const result = await host.agent({
      label: "init " + exp,
      input:
        deskNote +
        "Run exactly `" + cmd + "` from the quest worktree if " +
        "one is named above, else the repository root, and return " +
        "only its stdout JSON verdict verbatim as your entire " +
        "reply, with no prose and no code fences. If the command " +
        "fails, return its stdout JSON verdict verbatim instead. " +
        "Do not edit any file and do not call any `bp3 q u` " +
        "update edge.",
    });
    const v = parseVerdict(result);
    if (!v || v.ok !== true) {
      refusals.push(
        "record-init refused before the " + edge + " child: " +
        errorText(result)
      );
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  // The named tape binder (followup.3): this launcher, after
  // the child returns, when its session tape exists and has
  // closed. Resolution is mechanical — `bp3 harness
  // find-tape` on the run-id — and a resolution that is not
  // unique refuses typed, never a guess; the bind itself is
  // one pointer-only tape_binding row written by bind-tape.
  // The author child writes no binding.
  async function bindTape(edge, cycle) {
    const runId = runIdOf(edge, cycle);
    const resolveCmd =
      envPreset(edge, cycle) + "./bin/bp3 harness find-tape" +
      " --run-id " + runId;
    const resolved = await host.agent({
      label: "resolve " + exp,
      input:
        deskNote +
        "Run exactly `" + resolveCmd + "` from the quest worktree if " +
        "one is named above, else the repository root, and return " +
        "only its stdout JSON verdict verbatim as your entire " +
        "reply, with no prose and no code fences. If the command " +
        "fails, return its stdout JSON verdict verbatim instead. " +
        "Do not edit any file and do not call any `bp3 q u` " +
        "update edge.",
    });
    const rv = parseVerdict(resolved);
    const tapePath = rv && rv.ok === true
      ? (typeof rv.tape_path === "string" && rv.tape_path
         ? rv.tape_path
         : (typeof rv.wal === "string" ? rv.wal : ""))
      : "";
    if (!tapePath) {
      refusals.push(
        "bind-tape resolution refused after the " + edge + " child: " +
        errorText(resolved)
      );
      return false;
    }
    const bindCmd =
      envPreset(edge, cycle) + "./bin/bp3 harness bind-tape" +
      " --run-id " + runId + " --tape-path " + tapePath;
    const bound = await host.agent({
      label: "bind " + exp,
      input:
        deskNote +
        "Run exactly `" + bindCmd + "` from the quest worktree if " +
        "one is named above, else the repository root, and return " +
        "only its stdout JSON verdict verbatim as your entire " +
        "reply, with no prose and no code fences. If the command " +
        "fails, return its stdout JSON verdict verbatim instead. " +
        "Do not edit any file and do not call any `bp3 q u` " +
        "update edge.",
    });
    const bv = parseVerdict(bound);
    if (!bv || bv.ok !== true) {
      refusals.push(
        "bind-tape refused after the " + edge + " child: " +
        errorText(bound)
      );
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  function tapePreamble(edge, cycle) {
    const folder = runFolder(edge, cycle, harness + "-" + model);
    return (
      "Your run folder is `" + folder + "` under `" + expDir +
      "/runs/`. `BP3_RUN_ID`, `BP3_QUEST`, `BP3_EXP`, " +
      "`BP3_HARNESS`, and `BP3_MODEL` arrive via environment " +
      "and `bp3` stamps them into its verdicts and ledger " +
      "lines, so no first-command prefix is needed. First check whether that concrete run " +
      "folder already exists: if it does, stop immediately, do " +
      "not overwrite or reuse it, and return a JSON object " +
      '{"ok":false,"error":{"code":"E_RUN_EXISTS"}} describing ' +
      "the collision. Run-id folders must fail if they already " +
      "exist. Otherwise create the folder, then tee all of your " +
      "session output into its tape.log for the rest of the run: " +
      "run your shell work so stdout and stderr are appended " +
      "through `tee -a <run-folder>/tape.log` (for example " +
      "`exec > >(tee -a <run-folder>/tape.log) 2>&1` in bash, " +
      "or pipe each command through `tee -a`). The tape is " +
      "verbatim evidence only; never parse tape text into facts. " +
      "Write `<run-folder>/notes.md` with brief authored lessons " +
      "from the run before you finish. Record the concrete run " +
      "folder name as run_id in your reply JSON."
    );
  }

  const before = await readState();
  if (before.state === "unknown") {
    refusals.push("initial read failed: " + (before.raw || "no verdict"));
    return { exp: exp, outcome: "refused", commit: null, run_ids: runIds, refusals: refusals };
  }
  if (before.state !== "todo") {
    refusals.push(
      "expected todo, got " + before.state + "; another step owns that state"
    );
    return { exp: exp, outcome: "refused", commit: before.commit, run_ids: runIds, refusals: refusals };
  }

  if (!(await recordInit("handoff", before.cycle))) {
    return { exp: exp, outcome: "refused", commit: before.commit, run_ids: runIds, refusals: refusals };
  }

  const author = await host.agent({
    label: "author " + exp,
    input:
      deskNote + "You are the author child for exp `" + exp + "` of quest `" +
      quest + "`, currently in state `todo` at cycle " +
      String(before.cycle) + ". " + authorLoad + tapePreamble("handoff", before.cycle) +
      " Do the exp's work in the repository, then commit the " +
      "work as a clean git commit and note its full sha. Then " +
      "call the state edge directly yourself: " +
      "`" + envPreset("handoff", before.cycle) + "./bin/bp3 q " + quest + " u " + exp +
      " handoff --commit <your-commit-sha> --reason \"<short reason>\"`. " +
      "Children call `bp3 q u` directly; never only return a " +
      "verdict for the parent to relay. Reply with only a JSON " +
      "object {ok, run_id, commit, verdict} where verdict is " +
      "the JSON printed by the handoff call.",
  });
  const authorVerdict = parseVerdict(author);
  if (authorVerdict && typeof authorVerdict.run_id === "string" && authorVerdict.run_id) {
    runIds.push(authorVerdict.run_id);
  }

  // The child has returned and its session tape has closed:
  // bind it to the Run before re-reading state.
  await bindTape("handoff", before.cycle);

  const after = await readState();
  if (after.state === "handed_off") {
    const commit = after.commit
      ? String(after.commit)
      : (authorVerdict && authorVerdict.commit ? String(authorVerdict.commit) : null);
    return { exp: exp, outcome: "handed_off", commit: commit, run_ids: runIds, refusals: refusals };
  }
  refusals.push(errorText(author));
  if (after.state === "unknown") {
    refusals.push("re-read after author failed: " + (after.raw || "no verdict"));
  } else {
    refusals.push("author left state " + after.state + ", expected handed_off");
  }
  return {
    exp: exp,
    outcome: "refused",
    commit: after.commit === undefined ? null : after.commit,
    run_ids: runIds,
    refusals: refusals,
  };
}
